Well, it's been awhile ... I thought ascending a knight would be easy,
having ascended a monk and a tourist.  But it proved to be more
challenging than I thought.  Special notes here are that I never made a
teleport save through a trap, and never polymorphed anything, either
myself, something else, or an object.

Mostly my knights got killed through stupidity.  Quite a few made it
down to the medusa
level, where a monster-summoning titan killed quite a few of them. Then
I lost interest for several months.

Came back, and second knight ascended.

Important lessons:
-- even as dumb as a knight is,  blessing books (as someone here
suggested -- forget who but thank you!) allows you to use them
regardless of the low int score.

-- what caused me the most trouble was the lack of any missile weapons
for the knight in the early game. What solved it this time was that I
went down just to the first level of
the gnome mines just long enough to pick up a bow and liberate arrows
from an arrow trap. I chose arrows over daggers because A) with the
ring mail et al I was already carrying, I couldn't afford the weight
penalty B) rocks are heavy C) there are lots of arrow traps in the
dungeon, which allowed me to replenish my stock.   I even found some +2
arrows!   These served me until the valley of the dead, where I went
over to mmissile.

-- a big break for me was finding an early robe.  This allowed me to
learn "remove curse" at 0% and "identify" at 45% failure. This solved
my identity and cursing problems from the castle on. Also, since I
could do "remove curse" inherently, I got by with only carring ten
potions of holy water.  After all, since I could do the remove curse
myself, I only needed the water to move stuff from "uncursed" to
"bless" -- but that happens far less often.  I still carried some
scrolls of remove curse just in case.

-- best Thank you God! moment. Drop a ring down a sink ... which I know
I shouldn't do since I only have the one ... and it turns out to be a
ring of free action! I start kicking myself for throwing away something
so valuable when the next message is ...
"the sink backs up!"

Whoa!  I got my ring back! Bet that doesn't happen every day!

RNG was quite generous -- found 3 rings of conflict, 3 rings of
regeneration, 3 magic markers. It made up for it by only giving me the
guaranteed wand of death at orcus town ... the second one I had to burn
a wish for.

another discovery: I found that if you mix one potion of gain energy
with 5 potions of healing, the result is 5 potions of extra healing!
Did a lot of alchemy this way, pushing my HP up to a high number.

Stupid moments:

1)  Get down to castle level before it suddenly occurs to me that there
is such a thing
as magic lamps in the game. Rub one ... and sure enough, it is. POOF!
Hostile djinn.
Should've ID'd it some other way ... wasted wish!

2) while on ascension run, decide I need a ring slot. Without
thinking,start to pull off my ring of levitation ... then I remember
that I'm over water on Juiblex's level. There is water all around me.
If I do that, it's instant death.

I carefully move my hands away from the keyboard.

3) Same ascension run -- decide to eat a troll I just killed, forget to
notice I am satiated on the status line. When I saw the stop eating
prompt, I held back and THOUGHT about it for a few seconds before
hitting "n".  If I'd hit "y", I would have probably died right there.

Six wishes:
throne wish gives me cloak of magic resistance, which I use on the
quest.
castle wand has only 1 wish.  wish for 2 scrolls of genocide, which I
use to eliminate mind flayers and master mind flayers. recharge with
scroll
of charging.    Second wish for blessed book of identify.  Wait several
turns, do not find them in Gehennom, so burn third wish for blessed +2
fireproof boots of speed.

while dipping fountains, 2 water creatures give me two wishes. For the
first, I ask for
a wand of death. For the second, a +2 t-shirt to save polypiling for it
-- I couldn't find one.

Only found one wand of polymorph in game .. and wishes had already
given me everything I needed.  So I went polyless.  Magic resistance
prevented me from being
polyd by traps.

Went without teleport for most of game because I had no teleport
control.  When I finally found a ring of teleport control,  I decided
that I needed the additional ring slot more than I needed teleportitis.
So I did without it.  It did not prove to be much of a loss.

Also, my dog stepped on a poly trap and became a baby long worm, later
leveling to a long worm with 800 (!) hit points.  This would have been
better if he'd actually *attacked* anyone.    As it was, he was so
large it was impossible to get around him.
Plus his tail took up eight or so spaces, making it hard to get around
him.  I thought of using him as an organic wall, protecting me from the
bad guys while I used a halberd to stab them. I attempted it against
the boss on the quest level but it didn't work -- he was too clumsy. I
wound up leaving him on the bottom of the quest level.

